      "ownershipVehicle": "I-66 Blocker, LLC",
      "description": "I-66 Express Mobility Partners, LLC is the private concessionaire and operator of the 66 Express Outside the Beltway managed lanes in Northern Virginia, also known as Transform 66 Outside the Beltway. Under a 50-year DBFOM agreement with the Virginia Department of Transportation through 2066, the company financed, delivered, operates, and maintains a 22.5-mile corridor from I-495 to Route 29 in Gainesville. The approximately $3.7 billion project includes two express lanes and three rebuilt general-purpose lanes in each direction, interchange upgrades, more than 4,000 park-and-ride spaces, transit funding, and 18 miles of shared-use path. The full corridor opened ahead of schedule in November 2022. Ferrovial's audited 2025 filing reports Cintra at 55.7%, Meridiam Infrastructure S.a.r.l. at 29.75%, and I-66 Blocker (APG) at 14.55%.",
